1
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,000
(Blossom Through the Cloud)

2
00:01:35,001 --> 00:01:37,960
(Adapted from the novel on JJWXC,
"Landing on My Heart", by Qiao Yao)

3
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:45,640
I just got this tea cake.

4
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Give it a try.

5
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:01,320
I heard...

6
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,520
you're at loggerheads
with those old fogies again.

7
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:05,240
Not really.

8
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:07,800
It's just normal communication.

9
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:09,440
Enough. Don't give me that.

10
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:11,240
I'm advising you...

11
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:13,200
to just go along with them.

12
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:15,959
The shareholders' meeting is
coming up,

13
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:17,160
and things will be reshuffled.

14
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:18,840
At this critical juncture,

15
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:20,199
you should know
what's more important.

16
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:21,400
Think it through.

17
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:24,520
Dad.

18
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:28,200
Since when did our family
have to sacrifice...

19
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:30,120
a woman's career aspirations...

20
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:33,280
to consolidate our position
at the shareholders' meeting?

21
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:34,960
Wait.

22
00:02:34,961 --> 00:02:36,560
Aren't you planning
to marry her anyway?

23
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:39,400
If so, just do it sooner.

24
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:41,280
Can she still fly after marriage?

25
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:47,280
If marrying me
means she can no longer fly,

26
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:48,800
then why would I be confident...

27
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:50,040
that she will definitely marry me?

28
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:53,720
Regarding this matter,

29
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,400
you should just leave it
to me to handle.

30
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:01,840
The tea is good,

31
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:03,760
but it's a bit too hot.

32
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,360
Drink it yourself.

33
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:10,960
Not quite there yet.

34
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:16,160
(Episode 21: Some Endings
Precede the Next Chapter)

35
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:39,359
Hello, I'm Lu Zheng Yang,
an investigator...

36
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:41,280
from Hengshi Air's Safety Committee.

37
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:42,400
This is my ID.

38
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:44,240
These three are members
of the investigation team.

39
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:45,600
We've called
this emergency meeting...

40
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:47,800
to investigate the incident
in which Flight 5123...

41
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:49,880
failed to vacate the runway...

42
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,360
within the available
landing distance.

43
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:52,840
I'm Ruan Si Xian.

44
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:55,520
On Flight 5123
bound for Jiangcheng,

45
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:58,160
I was in the right seat,
the Pilot Monitoring (PM).

46
00:03:58,680 --> 00:03:59,760
Due to the captain's incapacitation,

47
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:01,120
I declared a mayday...

48
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:02,480
and took over the controls,

49
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:03,680
becoming the Pilot Flying (PF).

50
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:06,200
At the time, the weather was severe.

51
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:07,800
Strong winds and moderate showers.

52
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:09,400
So...

53
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:12,520
What exactly would it take...

54
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:13,880
to make you change your mind?

55
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:15,719
Unless...

56
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:16,920
the sun rises from the west.

57
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:20,640
You're truly a woman
who can send people to the sky.

58
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:22,800
I can also send people
to their graves.

59
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:24,840
You don't want to be my boss,

60
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:26,440
but my boyfriend?

61
00:04:28,280 --> 00:04:29,320
You're better off dreaming.

62
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:31,639
If I'm judging how well
a refrigerator cools,

63
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:33,520
do I have to sit inside it
for two days?

64
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:45,600
Mr. Fu.

65
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:48,440
Mr. Fu.

66
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:50,440
They've all arrived.

67
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:52,080
- Hello?
- Fu Ming Yu.

68
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:54,519
Can you let my mom
see Ms. Ruan tonight?

69
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:55,560
Otherwise, she won't be at ease.

70
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:56,800
We're almost there.

71
00:05:57,880 --> 00:05:58,880
Okay.

72
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,000
I understand.

73
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:03,560
Okay.

74
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:04,840
So what did he say?

75
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,160
- Go to Hengshi.
- Here's what.

76
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:09,480
I'll head back first.

77
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:10,880
You handle things at the airport.

78
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:12,320
Got it. Don't worry.

79
00:06:13,320 --> 00:06:14,320
Turn around.

80
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Ms. Dong, over here.

81
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:42,240
Ming Yu,

82
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:43,960
didn't she just...

83
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:45,520
land the plane successfully...

84
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:47,160
and save everyone on board?

85
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:49,440
Why is she still being investigated?

86
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:51,240
She...

87
00:06:51,241 --> 00:06:52,680
won't be punished, will she?

88
00:06:54,760 --> 00:06:56,080
This is all standard procedure.

89
00:06:56,760 --> 00:06:57,960
Ms. Dong, don't worry.

90
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:04,280
I rarely see her in her uniform.

91
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:06,600
She looks so good.

92
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:08,800
So beautiful and sharp.

93
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:11,160
I never imagined
such a petite person...

94
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:14,080
could actually fly
such a massive aircraft,

95
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:15,880
carrying passengers everywhere.

96
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:18,440
And at the critical moment,

97
00:07:19,320 --> 00:07:20,320
she managed to save the day.

98
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:23,160
She's truly remarkable.

99
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:26,720
You know,

100
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:28,800
her name...

101
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,560
was supposed to be Ruan Guang Zhi.

102
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:33,720
Doesn't it sound strange?

103
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:36,600
I remember when I was pregnant,

104
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:39,520
she was so active in my belly.

105
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:41,880
The experienced elders
around me said...

106
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:43,480
it must be a boy.

107
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:46,240
Her father was so eager...

108
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:47,400
to give her a name.

109
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:49,160
"With a calm mind
and great ambition,"

110
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:50,680
"what is there to fear?"

111
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:53,560
Then why did she get
her current name?

112
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:55,480
Back then,

113
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:56,800
when I was pregnant with her,

114
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:58,800
her father...

115
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:01,120
was transferred by his school
to teach in a frontier region.

116
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:03,080
It was a small...

117
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:04,920
and remote place.

118
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:07,800
The whole village
had only one phone.

119
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:09,920
So her father...

120
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:11,440
wrote letters to me.

121
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:13,240
As time went by,

122
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:15,440
I forgot most of what he wrote
in those letters.

123
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:17,480
I only remember...

124
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,160
that every letter ended...

125
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,200
with the words
"Thinking of you (Si Xian)."

126
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:24,920
I thought those two characters
were beautiful.

127
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:27,160
So when she was born,

128
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:28,880
I gave her that name.

129
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,040
It's a lovely name.

130
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:34,720
And then?

131
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:37,000
- What happened after that?
- Later...

132
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:40,520
To further my studies abroad
and continue painting,

133
00:08:41,560 --> 00:08:43,040
I had an amicable divorce
with her father.

134
00:08:43,920 --> 00:08:45,280
She has always refused to accept me.

135
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:48,480
I sent her child support,

136
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:50,360
but she wouldn't take a single cent.

137
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,120
She's very stubborn.

138
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:54,360
She's definitely like me
in that regard.

139
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:56,720
Then, after her father passed away,

140
00:08:57,800 --> 00:08:58,800
she was all alone,

141
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:00,400
studying...

142
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,240
while working part-time.

143
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:04,120
Such a young girl,

144
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:07,200
stumbling through life,

145
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:09,960
somehow managed to grow up.

146
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:13,120
I know...

147
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,760
she must have suffered a lot.

148
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:18,840
So Ming Yu,

149
00:09:20,760 --> 00:09:22,400
please treat her well from now on.

150
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:26,680
She has really had a hard time.

151
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:32,880
Don't worry.

152
00:09:37,240 --> 00:09:39,040
If anything had
really happened to her today,

153
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:41,480
I don't think I would ever
be able to forgive myself.

154
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:47,880
All right.

155
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:49,200
Enough of that.

156
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:50,960
I'll be heading back now.

157
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:52,720
Ms. Dong,

158
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:55,440
aren't you going
to wait for Ruan Ruan?

159
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:58,080
No need.

160
00:09:58,920 --> 00:10:00,400
Seeing her sitting there
safe and sound...

161
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:02,800
is enough to put my mind at ease.

162
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:05,160
Besides, she must
be exhausted today.

163
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:07,840
Let her go home
and get some good rest later.

164
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:10,720
Okay.

165
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:34,800
We're finished, right?

166
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:36,200
Thank you
for your hard work, everyone.

167
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:37,720
Xiao Ruan.

168
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:40,200
How are you doing?
Are you feeling all right?

169
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:41,560
I'm fine.

170
00:10:41,880 --> 00:10:42,880
How's Captain Yue?

171
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:44,639
He'll be fine.

172
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:46,800
He has a history of
vasovagal syncope.

173
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:48,120
It's in the flight surgeon's
records.

174
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:50,920
This time, it was likely triggered
by a sudden nosebleed.

175
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:54,320
Vasovagal what?

176
00:10:56,280 --> 00:10:59,360
Vasovagal syncope.

177
00:10:59,760 --> 00:11:01,000
You can just think of it
as fainting at blood.

178
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:05,720
Will he be able
to continue flying in the future?

179
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:07,160
He'll be fine once he recovers.

180
00:11:07,560 --> 00:11:09,440
But from now on, he'll be
on the priority checkup list.

181
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,520
All right. Don't worry so much.

182
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:13,040
Get some good rest.

183
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:15,679
Thank you
for your hard work, everyone.

184
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:16,680
I'll see you out.

185
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:12,560
Ruan Ruan!

186
00:12:26,360 --> 00:12:27,720
All right, stop crying.

187
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:32,239
It's one thing for Xiao Zhen to cry,

188
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:33,240
but why are you crying too?

189
00:12:33,480 --> 00:12:34,520
I'm not crying.

190
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:36,200
I'm just...

191
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:37,920
happy.

192
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:39,839
Otherwise, I thought my bar...

193
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:41,920
was about to lose
a source of free labor.

194
00:12:42,040 --> 00:12:43,760
I'm just so happy that you're here.

195
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,760
All right. Go home and rest.

196
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:48,120
It's been a long day.

197
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:49,560
Go home and get some sleep.

198
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Go on.

199
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:58,000
- Fu... Mr. Fu.
- Mr. Fu.

200
00:12:58,720 --> 00:12:59,720
Go on home.

201
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:04,040
- Bye, brother-in-law!
- Bye, brother-in-law!

202
00:13:12,840 --> 00:13:14,439
Wait, should I call him
brother-in-law?

203
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:15,880
Should it be
younger brother-in-law?

204
00:13:16,760 --> 00:13:17,800
The boss gave us instructions.

205
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:18,920
He told us to call him
brother-in-law.

206
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:21,400
Then brother-in-law it is.

207
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:23,640
- Let's go get some rest too.
- Let's go.

208
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:28,840
Stop laughing,

209
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:30,440
Ruan Guang Zhi.

210
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:34,560
No way.

211
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:36,320
She told you that too?

212
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:37,360
It's a nice name.

213
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:39,080
It has a deep meaning.

214
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:40,800
I'll call you Guang Zhi from now on.

215
00:13:43,120 --> 00:13:44,120
I tried so hard to keep it a secret,

216
00:13:44,440 --> 00:13:45,440
but I still failed.

217
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:47,720
But...

218
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:49,320
I really didn't expect her to come.

219
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,160
Back then,
for parent-teacher meetings...

220
00:13:51,360 --> 00:13:52,360
and graduation ceremonies,

221
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:54,480
even though I knew
she wouldn't show up,

222
00:13:55,640 --> 00:13:56,679
I still wondered...

223
00:13:56,680 --> 00:13:57,840
if she would give me a surprise.

224
00:13:58,840 --> 00:14:00,160
But every time, I was disappointed.

225
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:02,880
So eventually, I just
stopped expecting anything.

226
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:11,600
So "Captain" Ruan,
in those final minutes,

227
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:13,320
what were you thinking about?

228
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:17,240
Thinking about
how to land the plane safely.

229
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:25,640
But once I landed,

230
00:14:26,640 --> 00:14:27,640
the first person I thought of...

231
00:14:28,800 --> 00:14:29,800
was you.

232
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:34,120
I'm flattered.

233
00:14:36,160 --> 00:14:38,400
I wondered if you were still mad.

234
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:41,040
I saved a plane for you...

235
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:43,280
and prevented a major loss.

236
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:45,719
I didn't know...

237
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:46,800
if that would appease you.

238
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:57,400
What are you doing?

239
00:14:57,520 --> 00:14:58,520
Reflecting on my mistakes.

240
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:00,960
That's a good attitude.

241
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:03,920
It will never happen again.

242
00:15:05,520 --> 00:15:06,559
What won't?

243
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:07,880
I'll never leave home
in a huff again.

244
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:10,840
I won't let you...

245
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:12,440
carry our problems onto the plane.

246
00:15:12,680 --> 00:15:14,440
And I won't let you
have any unhappiness...

247
00:15:14,920 --> 00:15:17,200
or regrets
before you board a flight.

248
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:18,920
What if we have
an unfinished argument...

249
00:15:19,280 --> 00:15:20,600
before a flight?

250
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:21,720
I'll surrender unconditionally.

251
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:24,160
That won't do. That's not fair.

252
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:28,080
No matter what, I'll take the blame.

253
00:15:28,240 --> 00:15:29,759
As long as you bring me back...

254
00:15:29,760 --> 00:15:31,000
some souvenirs
from the cities you visit,

255
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:32,800
that'll be enough.

256
00:15:32,801 --> 00:15:33,880
Anyway, it can't be like today.

257
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:36,040
Wrong answer.

258
00:15:36,280 --> 00:15:37,920
The heroic "Captain" Ruan...

259
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:39,480
would never be the one at fault.

260
00:15:40,480 --> 00:15:41,720
You had better be careful.

261
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:43,880
Haven't you checked your phone yet?

262
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:46,680
I'm famous now.

263
00:15:47,440 --> 00:15:48,440
Let's break up.

264
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:50,240
I'm going to find
an "older guy" of my own.

265
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:53,000
An "older guy"?

266
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:55,400
Isn't that me?

267
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:57,320
No, you're not.

268
00:15:57,840 --> 00:15:59,200
You're the "brother-in-law".

269
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:03,360
What?

270
00:16:03,480 --> 00:16:04,680
Is our "brother-in-law"
tired of driving?

271
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:07,840
"Brother-in-law" has
unlimited stamina.

272
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:09,680
I can keep going
even after we get home.

273
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:13,400
What are you saying?

274
00:17:08,040 --> 00:17:09,040
Visual reference in sight.

275
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:10,280
Autopilot disconnected.

276
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:18,800
Spoilers. Reverse green. Decelerate.

277
00:17:23,240 --> 00:17:24,400
If I don't take responsibility,
who will?

278
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:25,800
I'm the Pilot-in-Command.

279
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:29,439
If you are in my position one day,
you'll do the same.

280
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:31,359
As a pilot, we must put...

281
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:33,279
the safety of the passengers
and property...

282
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:34,360
above all else.

283
00:17:34,560 --> 00:17:36,080
I would do it again anytime.

284
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:37,880
And I don't regret it at all.

285
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:21,000
I still woke you up.

286
00:18:23,360 --> 00:18:24,360
I wasn't sound asleep.

287
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:26,880
I have to go to the office today.

288
00:18:30,440 --> 00:18:31,480
Will I be grounded?

289
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:37,320
Don't think too much about it.

290
00:18:37,920 --> 00:18:38,920
Just get some rest today.

291
00:18:41,280 --> 00:18:42,320
Don't keep it from me this time.

292
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:45,400
Whether I'm grounded or not,

293
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:48,200
you must tell me immediately.

294
00:19:04,280 --> 00:19:05,280
No matter what happens,

295
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:07,480
you have to remember...

296
00:19:08,240 --> 00:19:09,240
that I'm here for you.

297
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:26,120
Go on.

298
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:27,360
Get some good sleep.

299
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:48,920
What a joke.

300
00:19:49,520 --> 00:19:52,080
Everyone, since when did
Hengshi's flight safety standards...

301
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:55,000
start being decided by netizens?

302
00:19:55,120 --> 00:19:57,680
You should be glad
that it didn't turn into a disaster.

303
00:19:58,200 --> 00:19:59,520
If anything had gone wrong,

304
00:19:59,760 --> 00:20:01,280
imagine how the netizens
would bash us.

305
00:20:01,520 --> 00:20:03,800
This Hengshi Tower would
be drowned in their spit.

306
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:08,040
We're not questioning
the female pilot's skills.

307
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:09,640
But in that situation,

308
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:11,040
she clearly could have woken up...

309
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,200
the unconscious captain.

310
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:13,960
That would have ensured...

311
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:15,160
a safer landing.

312
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:17,360
The captain just fainted
from seeing blood.

313
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:18,680
It wasn't anything serious.

314
00:20:18,681 --> 00:20:21,360
Then why did she insist
on landing the plane herself?

315
00:20:21,680 --> 00:20:23,560
Was she being overconfident?

316
00:20:24,280 --> 00:20:25,320
Or was she just...

317
00:20:26,040 --> 00:20:27,400
too eager...

318
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:29,159
to make a name for herself?

319
00:20:29,160 --> 00:20:30,799
I heard that not long ago,

320
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:32,760
she failed
her captain promotion exam.

321
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:35,240
And the inspector was
this very Captain Yue Yang.

322
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:37,159
If that's the case,

323
00:20:37,160 --> 00:20:38,760
then where did she put...

324
00:20:39,280 --> 00:20:40,280
the safety of the passengers?

325
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:42,640
Are you finished?

326
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:45,560
I have a question for all of you.

327
00:20:46,840 --> 00:20:48,040
Have you looked at the flight data?

328
00:20:52,680 --> 00:20:54,000
Since when did Hengshi...

329
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:56,480
stop using data
to evaluate standards...

330
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:58,320
and rely on assumptions instead?

331
00:20:59,080 --> 00:21:01,240
As for the pilot's state of mind
at the time,

332
00:21:01,840 --> 00:21:02,840
a person should be judged
by their actions,

333
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:04,439
not their intentions.

334
00:21:04,440 --> 00:21:05,840
We should look at the final result.

335
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:07,640
And the result is...

336
00:21:08,360 --> 00:21:11,000
that under such severe
weather conditions,

337
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:13,040
this pilot successfully
completed the landing,

338
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:15,600
ensuring the safety of
the passengers' lives and property.

339
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:17,200
There was no problem at all.

340
00:21:17,360 --> 00:21:19,520
Judge a person by their actions,
not their intentions.

341
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:21,680
Well said, Mr. Fu.

342
00:21:22,720 --> 00:21:24,720
You're going out of your way
to protect this female pilot.

343
00:21:25,840 --> 00:21:27,040
Is it because...

344
00:21:27,880 --> 00:21:29,640
of your special relationship
with her?

345
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:35,680
Our relationship...

346
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:37,680
has nothing to do
with this incident.

347
00:21:39,520 --> 00:21:42,680
Since you already have
a private, intimate relationship,

348
00:21:43,080 --> 00:21:46,240
then your stance
on this matter is biased.

349
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:48,520
So I think you should
recuse yourself, Mr. Fu.

350
00:21:48,800 --> 00:21:50,320
Just because she's my girlfriend,

351
00:21:50,960 --> 00:21:53,480
should she be treated unfairly
by everyone here?

352
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:55,680
This is easy to handle.

353
00:21:56,360 --> 00:21:57,479
It's just a suspension.

354
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:58,680
It's not a lifetime ban.

355
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:00,160
When this blows over,

356
00:22:00,440 --> 00:22:02,360
she can be retrained
and re-evaluated.

357
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:05,480
However, today's
suspension notice...

358
00:22:06,120 --> 00:22:08,040
must be issued by Mr. Fu himself.

359
00:22:08,480 --> 00:22:10,200
That way, you can prove...

360
00:22:10,320 --> 00:22:12,440
that you are not
being partial in this matter.

361
00:22:33,720 --> 00:22:35,240
I can tell you all very clearly.

362
00:22:35,960 --> 00:22:38,160
I will not issue
this suspension notice.

363
00:22:39,200 --> 00:22:40,200
First,

364
00:22:40,360 --> 00:22:41,560
issuing a suspension notice...

365
00:22:41,800 --> 00:22:42,800
would be unfair.

366
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:44,800
Second,

367
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:46,880
not issuing the notice...

368
00:22:47,520 --> 00:22:48,920
is what the public wants.

369
00:23:06,440 --> 00:23:08,119
"Those who said
female drivers are terrible,"

370
00:23:08,120 --> 00:23:09,319
"please step forward."

371
00:23:09,320 --> 00:23:11,040
"Let me see
if your face is red from shame."

372
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:14,520
"I thought the pilot
must have been a man."

373
00:23:14,720 --> 00:23:15,920
"I can't believe it's a woman."

374
00:23:18,560 --> 00:23:21,040
"Miss, what will it take
to marry you?"

375
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:23,199
"I thought she was pretty
when I saw her last time."

376
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:24,360
"I didn't expect her
to be so skilled."

377
00:23:24,520 --> 00:23:25,520
"She's amazing."

378
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:28,760
"I read the detailed report."

379
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:31,680
"They landed in heavy crosswinds
and torrential rain."

380
00:23:32,120 --> 00:23:33,120
"The runway was slippery,"

381
00:23:33,280 --> 00:23:34,280
"and the plane skidded."

382
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:35,560
"She stopped it at the last second."

383
00:23:35,840 --> 00:23:36,919
"I only have two words."

384
00:23:36,920 --> 00:23:37,920
"Pure genius."

385
00:23:38,640 --> 00:23:39,640
I'll stop. I can't read them all.

386
00:23:39,840 --> 00:23:41,120
There are
too many positive comments.

387
00:23:41,440 --> 00:23:42,440
So "Captain" Ruan,

388
00:23:42,600 --> 00:23:44,680
how does it feel
to be showered with such praise?

389
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:48,320
I'm not really affected.

390
00:23:49,360 --> 00:23:51,560
Because I was just doing my job.

391
00:23:52,960 --> 00:23:54,480
I don't care about that.

392
00:23:54,840 --> 00:23:56,800
All I know is
that "Captain" Ruan is famous again.

393
00:23:57,080 --> 00:23:58,520
You have to treat us to something.

394
00:23:59,560 --> 00:24:02,120
To be precise,
I'm back in the spotlight,

395
00:24:02,320 --> 00:24:03,680
since I was famous once before.

396
00:24:04,480 --> 00:24:06,400
As for the treat...

397
00:24:06,640 --> 00:24:07,640
Then...

398
00:24:08,560 --> 00:24:09,799
tonight's drinks...

399
00:24:09,800 --> 00:24:11,480
are all on "Captain" Ruan.

400
00:24:12,040 --> 00:24:13,240
The internet is right.

401
00:24:13,640 --> 00:24:14,640
The richer you are,
the stingier you get.

402
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:16,840
Aren't tonight's drinks
just these few glasses?

403
00:24:17,360 --> 00:24:18,879
What's wrong with a few drinks?

404
00:24:18,880 --> 00:24:20,200
Drink up! Drink as much as you want.

405
00:24:23,680 --> 00:24:25,680
Why do I get the feeling
that you're not very happy?

406
00:24:28,320 --> 00:24:29,440
It's just that...

407
00:24:30,480 --> 00:24:33,000
I don't know if this is
a blessing or a curse yet.

408
00:24:33,720 --> 00:24:35,280
Did you forget
what happened to my mentor?

409
00:24:37,200 --> 00:24:38,760
But you did so well.

410
00:24:38,920 --> 00:24:40,360
Does the Safety Committee
still need to investigate?

411
00:24:40,600 --> 00:24:41,600
I don't know.

412
00:24:41,960 --> 00:24:43,360
Now we're just waiting
for the results.

413
00:24:43,760 --> 00:24:44,760
It should be soon.

414
00:24:46,480 --> 00:24:47,759
What we're celebrating today...

415
00:24:47,760 --> 00:24:49,440
isn't your company's assessment
of your performance,

416
00:24:49,960 --> 00:24:51,640
nor whether you're a hero.

417
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:53,600
What are we celebrating today?

418
00:24:54,160 --> 00:24:55,160
It's the fact...

419
00:24:55,360 --> 00:24:56,360
that we've lived another day.

420
00:24:56,640 --> 00:24:57,840
You're a survivor.

421
00:24:58,080 --> 00:25:00,040
Ladies, isn't that
worth celebrating?

422
00:25:00,080 --> 00:25:01,320
- You're right.
- Cheers!

423
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:03,160
Cheers!

424
00:25:03,840 --> 00:25:05,000
You're absolutely right.

425
00:25:05,200 --> 00:25:06,480
Tong Le, music!

426
00:25:06,760 --> 00:25:07,760
Let's get this party started!

427
00:25:07,920 --> 00:25:08,920
Dong!

428
00:25:11,320 --> 00:25:12,480
Come on!

429
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:31,200
Let's dance together!

430
00:25:31,840 --> 00:25:32,840
Let's dance!

431
00:26:44,440 --> 00:26:45,840
So where should we start?

432
00:26:46,720 --> 00:26:47,920
We need to improve efficiency.

433
00:26:48,400 --> 00:26:50,000
Reforming the QAR is
a matter of urgency.

434
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:51,480
So what do we need?

435
00:26:52,080 --> 00:26:53,160
We need to convince them...

436
00:26:53,360 --> 00:26:54,960
both empirically and emotionally...

437
00:26:55,200 --> 00:26:56,440
that we can change this.

438
00:26:57,120 --> 00:26:58,120
Think about it.
What we need are pilots.

439
00:26:59,560 --> 00:27:00,720
Pilots are human beings.

440
00:27:00,960 --> 00:27:01,960
I heard...

441
00:27:02,040 --> 00:27:03,360
the board is forcing Mr. Fu...

442
00:27:03,640 --> 00:27:05,080
to issue your grounding notice.

443
00:27:05,520 --> 00:27:06,960
Mr. Fu has been holding out
against them.

444
00:27:08,240 --> 00:27:09,800
This also seems to involve...

445
00:27:10,120 --> 00:27:11,200
interests between shareholders.

446
00:27:11,800 --> 00:27:13,680
Anyway, Mr. Fu has been...

447
00:27:14,040 --> 00:27:15,160
under considerable pressure lately.

448
00:27:17,080 --> 00:27:18,720
Okay, I understand.

449
00:27:35,760 --> 00:27:37,200
You have to trust him.

450
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:39,080
I'm a good example.

451
00:27:39,400 --> 00:27:40,960
Being grounded might not
be a bad thing.

452
00:27:41,280 --> 00:27:42,359
An early grounding...

453
00:27:42,360 --> 00:27:43,640
might lead
to an early return to flight.

454
00:27:43,840 --> 00:27:45,200
Don't let it wear you down.

455
00:27:46,120 --> 00:27:47,319
If you're really bored,

456
00:27:47,320 --> 00:27:48,479
come over to my place...

457
00:27:48,480 --> 00:27:49,480
and help me look after the kids.

458
00:27:51,800 --> 00:27:52,800
Okay, Captain Fan.

459
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:56,919
It's just that those people
on the board...

460
00:27:56,920 --> 00:27:58,200
won't let go of your relationship.

461
00:27:59,080 --> 00:28:00,120
But don't worry, Xiao Ruan.

462
00:28:00,440 --> 00:28:01,960
Mr. Fu will find a way
to resolve it.

463
00:28:02,920 --> 00:28:03,920
That's all for now. Don't worry.

464
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:06,520
Okay, I understand.

465
00:28:20,440 --> 00:28:22,240
I'm a bit busy today.
I'm not finished yet.

466
00:28:23,160 --> 00:28:24,440
Don't wait up for me. Get some rest.

467
00:28:24,640 --> 00:28:26,599
(Fu Ming Yu)

468
00:28:26,600 --> 00:28:35,720
(Is the discussion not going well?)

469
00:28:42,440 --> 00:28:44,400
Okay. You should get some rest too.

470
00:29:20,280 --> 00:29:21,400
To meet someone like you,

471
00:29:22,480 --> 00:29:23,480
I'm already very content.

472
00:29:25,280 --> 00:29:26,280
But...

473
00:29:26,840 --> 00:29:28,080
if we weren't together,

474
00:29:29,120 --> 00:29:30,120
then you wouldn't be...

475
00:29:30,680 --> 00:29:31,720
in such a dilemma, would you?

476
00:29:39,040 --> 00:29:40,040
You see me every day.

477
00:29:40,640 --> 00:29:41,640
Aren't you tired of looking yet?

478
00:29:44,600 --> 00:29:45,600
I can't get enough.

479
00:29:46,960 --> 00:29:47,960
I'll never get enough.

480
00:29:56,760 --> 00:29:57,760
When did you get back?

481
00:30:03,760 --> 00:30:04,800
If I remember correctly,

482
00:30:06,400 --> 00:30:07,400
it was around 4 am.

483
00:30:08,160 --> 00:30:09,160
Something like that.

484
00:30:09,600 --> 00:30:10,600
Did everything...

485
00:30:11,400 --> 00:30:12,400
go smoothly?

486
00:30:16,560 --> 00:30:17,560
You promised me.

487
00:30:19,520 --> 00:30:20,600
No matter what the outcome is,

488
00:30:22,360 --> 00:30:23,520
you'll tell me the truth.

489
00:30:31,760 --> 00:30:32,920
It really wasn't that smooth.

490
00:30:33,480 --> 00:30:34,480
But it's okay.

491
00:30:36,040 --> 00:30:37,120
Give me a little more time.

492
00:30:38,080 --> 00:30:39,440
I can handle this.

493
00:30:41,040 --> 00:30:42,040
Trust me.

494
00:30:49,600 --> 00:30:50,800
Do you have any plans for today?

495
00:30:56,760 --> 00:30:57,840
Today,

496
00:31:02,080 --> 00:31:03,200
I want to go on a date with you.

497
00:31:06,000 --> 00:31:07,000
A date?

498
00:31:07,960 --> 00:31:09,360
Like a normal young couple.

499
00:31:11,280 --> 00:31:12,560
We were both too busy before.

500
00:31:13,840 --> 00:31:15,600
We never had time for a proper date.

501
00:31:20,320 --> 00:31:21,720
Then I won't
schedule any work today.

502
00:31:23,040 --> 00:31:24,040
Let's go on a date.

503
00:31:25,680 --> 00:31:26,680
Where do you want to go?

504
00:31:30,040 --> 00:31:31,040
The amusement park.

505
00:31:48,240 --> 00:31:49,240
Slow down.

506
00:31:49,960 --> 00:31:50,960
Don't fall.

507
00:32:01,160 --> 00:32:02,160
That wasn't exciting enough.

508
00:32:03,800 --> 00:32:04,960
Let's go on the roller coaster.

509
00:32:05,360 --> 00:32:06,360
The roller coaster?

510
00:32:20,880 --> 00:32:21,880
Are you okay?

511
00:32:22,600 --> 00:32:23,600
Not really.

512
00:33:24,800 --> 00:33:26,120
The sunset is beautiful today.

513
00:33:30,720 --> 00:33:32,480
Hey, you two! Want to take a photo?

514
00:33:32,760 --> 00:33:33,760
It'll be ready in an instant.

515
00:33:33,960 --> 00:33:35,320
The lighting is perfect right now.

516
00:33:35,800 --> 00:33:37,760
Couples look great
in photos like this.

517
00:33:38,920 --> 00:33:39,920
- Why don't...
- Let's take one.

518
00:33:40,720 --> 00:33:41,720
Take one.

519
00:33:42,360 --> 00:33:43,479
- Okay.
- Great.

520
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:44,600
Face this way.

521
00:33:45,800 --> 00:33:46,800
Come on.

522
00:33:46,960 --> 00:33:47,960
Get closer.

523
00:33:48,640 --> 00:33:51,000
Three, two, one.

524
00:33:55,160 --> 00:33:56,640
- Take a look.
- Does it print right away?

525
00:33:56,920 --> 00:33:58,600
- Let me take another one.
- Okay.

526
00:33:58,800 --> 00:34:00,080
- One more.
- Okay, change your pose.

527
00:34:00,680 --> 00:34:02,880
Three, two, one.

528
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:09,680
- It looks great.
- Let me pay for it.

529
00:34:09,920 --> 00:34:10,920
Okay, thank you.

530
00:34:12,640 --> 00:34:13,679
All right.

531
00:34:13,680 --> 00:34:14,839
Thank you.

532
00:34:14,840 --> 00:34:15,879
It's ready.

533
00:34:15,880 --> 00:34:16,880
- It's pretty.
- It's really nice.

534
00:34:19,080 --> 00:34:20,840
I don't have pockets. You keep it.

535
00:34:28,720 --> 00:34:30,240
The sunset is quite beautiful today.

536
00:34:32,640 --> 00:34:34,240
I haven't seen
such a beautiful sunset...

537
00:34:34,320 --> 00:34:35,320
in a long time.

538
00:34:35,920 --> 00:34:37,720
I always feel
like I'm in such a hurry.

539
00:34:39,080 --> 00:34:41,440
Even though I can
see the sunset from the sky,

540
00:34:42,240 --> 00:34:44,960
without the sea breeze
and the waves,

541
00:34:45,720 --> 00:34:47,040
it just feels quite ordinary.

542
00:34:47,880 --> 00:34:49,360
Maybe one day,
when I can't fly anymore,

543
00:34:50,520 --> 00:34:51,520
I'll miss the days...

544
00:34:51,960 --> 00:34:52,960
of watching the sunset...

545
00:34:53,440 --> 00:34:54,480
from the cockpit.

546
00:35:03,120 --> 00:35:04,240
Why would you suddenly say...

547
00:35:04,720 --> 00:35:05,720
you can't fly anymore?

548
00:35:07,760 --> 00:35:08,760
I'll retire eventually.

549
00:35:09,600 --> 00:35:10,600
Otherwise,

550
00:35:11,280 --> 00:35:13,200
do you expect me to work for you
for the rest of my life?

551
00:35:21,360 --> 00:35:22,520
Why are you so nervous?

552
00:35:22,960 --> 00:35:23,960
I'm not.

553
00:35:25,160 --> 00:35:26,160
I'm not nervous at all.

554
00:35:27,040 --> 00:35:28,040
I'm very relaxed.

555
00:35:29,600 --> 00:35:30,600
Very relaxed.

556
00:35:32,400 --> 00:35:33,400
Fine.

557
00:35:34,040 --> 00:35:35,040
You're the most relaxed person.

558
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:01,000
Fu Ming Yu.

559
00:36:04,840 --> 00:36:05,880
After the sun sets...

560
00:36:12,160 --> 00:36:13,480
The sun hasn't set yet.

561
00:36:35,440 --> 00:36:36,440
The sun has set.

562
00:36:38,120 --> 00:36:39,640
- Let's...
- I know what you're going to say.

563
00:36:40,600 --> 00:36:41,600
I don't agree.

564
00:36:45,760 --> 00:36:46,760
I told you,

565
00:36:47,560 --> 00:36:49,160
I can handle everything.

566
00:36:50,840 --> 00:36:51,960
I need you to trust me.

567
00:36:54,760 --> 00:36:55,760
I'm just tired.

568
00:36:57,840 --> 00:37:00,080
Do you know how hard
the first half of my life has been?

569
00:37:00,640 --> 00:37:03,600
Do you know how hard I've worked
for this career?

570
00:37:07,400 --> 00:37:08,400
Maybe...

571
00:37:09,680 --> 00:37:10,960
this is fate's way of telling us...

572
00:37:12,880 --> 00:37:13,880
that we're not meant to be.

573
00:37:16,920 --> 00:37:18,360
Actually, I think it's better
if we part ways.

574
00:37:19,840 --> 00:37:21,120
You won't have to be
in a bind anymore,

575
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:23,240
and I won't have to struggle either.

576
00:37:24,240 --> 00:37:25,919
- Really.
- Whether we're compatible or not...

577
00:37:25,920 --> 00:37:27,360
should be up to us to decide.

578
00:37:27,960 --> 00:37:28,960
Ruan Si Xian,

579
00:37:29,560 --> 00:37:32,119
you don't need
to care about anything...

580
00:37:32,120 --> 00:37:33,280
other than our relationship.

581
00:37:33,520 --> 00:37:34,920
Why don't you understand?

582
00:37:35,360 --> 00:37:36,480
If we weren't together,

583
00:37:36,760 --> 00:37:39,040
these problems wouldn't even exist.

584
00:37:40,400 --> 00:37:41,760
I love my flying career.

585
00:37:42,960 --> 00:37:44,000
I love it even more...

586
00:37:44,960 --> 00:37:46,600
than our relationship.

587
00:37:46,840 --> 00:37:47,959
I want to start over.

588
00:37:47,960 --> 00:37:49,400
I don't want it to end like this.

589
00:37:53,200 --> 00:37:54,200
Actually, I think...

590
00:37:54,480 --> 00:37:55,760
parting on good terms is
for the best.

591
00:37:57,200 --> 00:37:58,200
Look.

592
00:37:59,560 --> 00:38:00,600
The sunset is so beautiful today.

593
00:38:02,080 --> 00:38:03,080
It's like...

594
00:38:04,440 --> 00:38:06,800
it's drawing
a perfect ending for us.

595
00:38:15,240 --> 00:38:16,640
Issue the grounding notice soon.

596
00:38:18,360 --> 00:38:19,360
The sooner it's issued,

597
00:38:20,920 --> 00:38:21,920
the sooner I can fly again.

598
00:38:25,320 --> 00:38:26,400
Didn't you promise me...

599
00:38:27,560 --> 00:38:28,880
that you wouldn't just discard me?

600
00:38:29,360 --> 00:38:30,560
Don't be childish.

601
00:38:33,160 --> 00:38:35,520
Anyone or anything
that gets in the way of my flying...

602
00:38:37,320 --> 00:38:39,160
will be thrown away
like trash by me.

603
00:38:46,080 --> 00:38:47,080
Si Xian.

604
00:38:47,360 --> 00:38:48,360
Ruan Si Xian!

605
00:39:57,680 --> 00:39:58,680
Hello, ma'am.

606
00:40:10,360 --> 00:40:11,360
Coming.

607
00:40:12,120 --> 00:40:13,120
Ruan Ruan.

608
00:40:14,200 --> 00:40:16,080
What took you so long? Come in.

609
00:40:17,040 --> 00:40:18,040
Help me tidy up.

610
00:40:25,680 --> 00:40:27,000
What's with that look?

611
00:40:27,560 --> 00:40:29,200
Shouldn't you congratulate me
on my move?

612
00:40:29,880 --> 00:40:31,480
Congratulate you on moving
from a luxury apartment...

613
00:40:31,720 --> 00:40:33,480
to this old shack?

614
00:40:33,680 --> 00:40:35,439
No matter how luxurious
Mingchen Apartments is,

615
00:40:35,440 --> 00:40:36,480
it isn't mine.

616
00:40:36,880 --> 00:40:37,880
But this is my home.

617
00:40:40,360 --> 00:40:41,360
I finally...

618
00:40:42,280 --> 00:40:44,040
bought back the house
that my father left me.

619
00:40:44,720 --> 00:40:45,720
I guess you could say...

620
00:40:45,880 --> 00:40:47,600
I've achieved a small goal of mine.

621
00:40:48,320 --> 00:40:49,840
I know that's true,

622
00:40:50,040 --> 00:40:51,040
but I still can't smile about it.

623
00:40:51,520 --> 00:40:52,840
You worked so hard,

624
00:40:53,160 --> 00:40:54,960
only to end up in this state.

625
00:40:55,280 --> 00:40:57,560
That's why I asked you over
to help me decorate.

626
00:40:59,160 --> 00:41:00,680
I think my home is quite nice.

627
00:41:01,200 --> 00:41:02,600
Don't look down on it for being old.

628
00:41:03,240 --> 00:41:05,600
The layout and the natural light
are both excellent.

629
00:41:05,960 --> 00:41:06,960
Besides,

630
00:41:08,160 --> 00:41:09,200
as soon as I walked in,

631
00:41:10,200 --> 00:41:11,600
it felt so familiar and warm.

632
00:41:14,120 --> 00:41:15,120
It's like my dad...

633
00:41:16,600 --> 00:41:17,640
is right here with me.

634
00:41:22,400 --> 00:41:23,400
Mr. Ruan?

635
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:25,520
Is he here with you?

636
00:41:28,560 --> 00:41:29,560
Hello, Mr. Ruan.

637
00:41:30,560 --> 00:41:32,000
You look like a kind man.

638
00:41:32,280 --> 00:41:35,080
I'm sure you wouldn't suddenly
jump out and scare me, right?

639
00:41:35,440 --> 00:41:36,440
Why are you so nervous?

640
00:41:37,880 --> 00:41:39,080
It was just a metaphor.

641
00:41:39,480 --> 00:41:41,120
Look at how scared you are.
Get to work.

642
00:41:43,920 --> 00:41:45,720
I thought you called me over
for something good.

643
00:41:46,160 --> 00:41:48,160
First, Xuan orders me around,
and now you're doing it too.

644
00:41:48,400 --> 00:41:50,120
I'm just a workhorse
for the two of you.

645
00:41:50,920 --> 00:41:51,960
As long as you know your place.

646
00:42:15,040 --> 00:42:16,040
Actually,

647
00:42:18,720 --> 00:42:19,840
I've always felt...

648
00:42:21,640 --> 00:42:22,880
that Lu Ming is still by my side.

649
00:42:29,480 --> 00:42:31,040
When you almost had that accident,

650
00:42:31,560 --> 00:42:33,000
I was worried sick.

651
00:42:33,760 --> 00:42:35,240
I kept talking to Lu Ming.

652
00:42:35,760 --> 00:42:37,480
I said, "If you can hear me,"

653
00:42:37,800 --> 00:42:39,320
"please keep Ruan Ruan safe."

654
00:42:41,160 --> 00:42:43,200
Tell me, do you think he heard me?

655
00:42:49,480 --> 00:42:50,480
Thank you.

656
00:42:55,320 --> 00:42:57,400
Wasn't I being ridiculous and silly?

657
00:42:58,120 --> 00:42:59,120
It was clearly your own...

658
00:42:59,560 --> 00:43:00,680
excellent flying skills.

659
00:43:01,360 --> 00:43:02,360
I believe...

660
00:43:03,760 --> 00:43:05,160
many people helped me.

661
00:43:06,600 --> 00:43:07,600
Maybe it was my dad.

662
00:43:09,560 --> 00:43:10,560
Maybe it was Lu Ming.

663
00:43:16,080 --> 00:43:17,200
I've decided to move on too.

664
00:43:19,240 --> 00:43:20,240
After all,

665
00:43:20,960 --> 00:43:22,280
we can't live in the past forever.

666
00:43:24,240 --> 00:43:25,240
I want to look forward.

667
00:43:25,840 --> 00:43:26,840
For Lu Ming's sake,

668
00:43:28,240 --> 00:43:29,600
I want to see what the future holds.

669
00:43:48,800 --> 00:43:53,760
(Departing Ep. 21 for Ep. 22)
